  "note": "A Monte Carlo price comes with a standard error; a finite-difference price\ndoes not. On the disc and the ellipse the Cartesian grid cuts the barrier at\nplaces that depend on where the grid sits, so the price depends on the grid's\nposition as well as on its spacing. Translating the grid by a random fraction\nof a cell (uniform on [-1/2, 1/2)^2, spacing unchanged) turns that dependence\ninto a sample: K placements give K prices, and their spread is a statistical\nmeasure of the placement-dependent part of the discretisation error, with\nmean +- SD/sqrt(K) the analogue of a Monte Carlo mean +- SEM.",
